<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - DUTCH COMPANY RESULTS DUE NOV 18.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - DUTCH COMPANY RESULTS DUE NOV 18.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of Dutch</p>
<p>company results for week beginning Monday, Nov 18 include:</p>
<p>DATE--COMPANY-------PERIOD--PFT/DIV--CONSENSUS--RANGE-----PVS</p>
<p> 20/11 CSM	    YR 95/96   PFT    203.0   197.5-207  186.5</p>
<p> 21/11 ING*	    9M	  PFT   2340	2270-2553 1883</p>
<p>Profit figures are net profits before extraordinary items</p>
<p>and in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>Securities houses surveyed included: Amstgeld, Bangert</p>
<p>Pontier, BZW, Delta Lloyd Bank, Generale Bank, Kempen &amp; Co,</p>
<p>Labouchere, Lanschot Bankiers and Wesselius.</p>
<p>NOTE - Banks and brokers interested in contributing to</p>
<p>Reuters surveys can contact the Amsterdam newsroom on</p>
<p>+31-20-504-5000 or fax their forecasts to +31-20-504 5040.</p>
<p>For the week starting November 25 we are collecting Q3</p>
<p>result forecasts for Nedlloyd, Ahold and Fortis Amev.</p>
<p>Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (FAX 31-20-504-5040)</p>
</text>
